# Catalog and hub docs

`docs/repos.md` is the source of truth for where work belongs. Skills and rules point at it. They do not keep a second copy of the list.

When editing the catalog:

- Put current projects under `Active`.
- Put finished or coursework repositories under `Archive`.
- Open an archive repository only when the user names it or is continuing that specific project.
- Each active entry needs a name, URL, status, one-sentence purpose, and a "Open a chat here when" line.
- Write the purpose so a later chat can match a request to it without opening the other repository.
- Update the "Catalog checked" date when the list is refreshed from GitHub.
- Leave `README.md` (the GitHub profile) unchanged unless the user asks to change the profile.
